{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778944114,"nonce":"E+5MdaR09ykXPqgAWe8VNpDI9LA=","title":"Unified Chat/History workspace with conversation sidebar","message":"## Problem\nMandible currently treats live chat/console sessions and conversation history as separate top-level experiences. That creates duplicated UI, inconsistent rendering expectations, and an unnatural workflow: the user can browse history in one place, but must switch context to interact with or continue that conversation.\n\nThe desired product model is closer to modern chat apps and the Codex app: conversation history and active chat are the same workspace. A conversation can be read historically, then immediately continued if the transport supports it or if Mandible can launch/resume an agent session for it.\n\n## Product direction\nCreate a unified Chat workspace with:\n\n- a conversation sidebar listing conversation titles/history;\n- a main transcript/detail pane using the best shared renderer;\n- a composer at the bottom when the selected conversation/session can be continued;\n- transport-aware continuation behavior: send another message to an existing live session when possible, resume/open a session when needed, or create a new one if no active runtime exists;\n- clean handling of SDK, PTY/Claude Code CLI, Codex, Gemini, channel-connected sessions, and historical read-only conversations;\n- no separate History top-level tab once the unified workspace is complete.\n\nThe History view is closer to the desired information architecture than the current Chat/Console sub-tab model. The current Chat tab's sub-tabs for running sessions should become either sidebar state, conversation metadata, or transport/debug affordances inside the selected conversation, not the main navigation model.\n\n## UX expectations\n- Sidebar: conversation list with title, agent/provider, repo/branch/project, recency, live/idle/dead indicator, issue/work/auth badges where available.\n- Main pane: full transcript/history, using shared message components so live and historical transcripts look the same.\n- Composer: visible and enabled when Mandible knows how to continue the selected conversation; disabled/read-only with a clear reason otherwise.\n- Starting interaction from history should not feel like a mode switch. Typing should resume/open the needed runtime automatically if policy and transport allow it.\n- Running sessions should be visible, but not as chat sub-tabs. They are state attached to conversations.\n- Terminal/debug views remain available as secondary transport/debug panes when the selected conversation is PTY-backed or needs permission interaction.\n- The workspace should have intentional internal scroll regions; the whole Mandible view should not page-scroll or wiggle.\n\n## Backend/integration requirements\n- Conversation identity must be stable enough to bind history entries to live sessions without title matching. Use existing `history_conversation_id` / provider session linkage where applicable, and improve it if needed.\n- Conversation list should be backed by the conversations/session tables, not only live console sessions.\n- Sending a message should route through a transport adapter for the selected conversation: SDK, PTY/Claude Code CLI, Codex, Gemini, or future transports.\n- Resume/create behavior should be explicit and testable, including dead sessions and conversations whose provider session IDs are reused or ambiguous.\n- The work ledger should link issues/work units/auth evidence to conversations so the sidebar/detail pane can show useful context without graph-only navigation.\n- Starred chats/bookmarks should become filters or saved views within the unified workspace, not an isolated product surface unless there is a strong reason.\n\n## Relationship to ledger work\nThis is not strictly required for the ledger core, but it should influence the conversation/session parts of the ledger integration:\n\n- sessions are live runtime state;\n- conversations are durable user-facing history;\n- work units/issues/auth requests should link to conversations and sessions separately where both exist;\n- graph should treat live sessions as actor overlays and conversations as durable history/detail objects.\n\n## Related issues\n- 835e0bb — Resume live chat from history and audit Codex model presets.\n- 8546c2f — Chat follow-ups: transcript rehydration, terminal fallback, Gemini, model picker.\n- 2b03ed3 — Header restructure.\n- e8c1d43 — Ledger integration: work units, auth requests, sessions, commits.\n- 23b67b7 — Ledger UI: issue detail, comments, sync/conflict UX.\n\n## Verification\n- Browser smoke: select an old conversation, inspect history, type a new message, and verify Mandible resumes/opens the correct runtime.\n- Browser smoke: live session appears in the same sidebar/list as history, with status reflected.\n- Regression: conversations with shared provider session ID do not resume to the wrong transcript.\n- Regression: long resumed chats open at the latest messages when appropriate.\n- Regression: live and history renderers do not diverge visually.\n- Browser layout check: no top-level page scroll/wiggle; sidebar and transcript scroll intentionally.\n\n## Done means\nChat and History become one coherent workspace: history browsing, live session monitoring, and continued interaction all happen from the same conversation-centered surface, with transport/debug details secondary to the conversation itself.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}